    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Kashmir Saffron was granted the Geographical Indication (GI) tag in 2020 and is mainly cultivated in Pulwama (Pampore), Budgam, Srinagar, and Kishtwar.",
        "CSIR-IIIM (Indian Institute of Integrative Medicine) is located in Jammu and plays a key role in the Aroma Mission.",
        "Census 2011 demographic indicators (Sex Ratio: 889, Child Sex Ratio: 862, Density: 56 per sq km) are frequently asked in JKSSB and JKPSC exams."
      ],
